[{:db/id "q-10949/selection/f378dc08a7c5bd483d4c7c5dda8691a39690941d477baa5b9bb2347c484b0e73" :answer/id #uuid "f6323197-75d5-5798-a0f0-5cebf78339a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $I=(0,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10949/selection/3f6246b334b665fffd5f5c0aeb61ba8b395e155b752456238f49d1e7f909e694" :answer/id #uuid "9bc2cdb0-3689-5c36-9e68-d90929ab14d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R=\\infty $ and $I=(-\\infty ,\\infty )$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10949/selection/20a710281995c110f431442cb9259f4d535998f68b88440295a71026a973d6ca" :answer/id #uuid "434eaf26-d1a9-579b-8e14-849a65caf76c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $I=(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10949/selection/6cff2ebce6ff39eb5e58edc75fecf8d7971dca5047bced4567382cd8259cb6d4" :answer/id #uuid "9df29785-afed-5fe7-adb8-aa8062ab27a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R=2$ and $I=(-1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10949/selection/279070109672eda4d52ba1e6f9063b4cda5cc58c44de321f12aa3ffe98d3b105" :answer/id #uuid "7582e5b5-d637-566b-b7db-97b68fa9e306" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R=\\infty $ and $I=(-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10949/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8b5b4f1-d3f3-5f3a-92d9-af81785db125" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-10949/selection/3f6246b334b665fffd5f5c0aeb61ba8b395e155b752456238f49d1e7f909e694" :answer-field/choices ["q-10949/selection/f378dc08a7c5bd483d4c7c5dda8691a39690941d477baa5b9bb2347c484b0e73" "q-10949/selection/3f6246b334b665fffd5f5c0aeb61ba8b395e155b752456238f49d1e7f909e694" "q-10949/selection/20a710281995c110f431442cb9259f4d535998f68b88440295a71026a973d6ca" "q-10949/selection/6cff2ebce6ff39eb5e58edc75fecf8d7971dca5047bced4567382cd8259cb6d4" "q-10949/selection/279070109672eda4d52ba1e6f9063b4cda5cc58c44de321f12aa3ffe98d3b105"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-10949" :question/id #uuid "37e2ef5f-52a9-5810-a866-d25a6434c7cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-10949" :question/problem "Find the radius of convergence $R$ and interval of convergence $I$ for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{2}^{n}(x-1)^{n}}{n!}\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To apply the ratio test we define ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{2}^{n}(x-1)^{n}}{n!}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{2}^{n+1}(x-1)^{n+1}}{(n+1)!}\\cdot \\frac{n!}{{2}^{n}(x-1)^{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{2(x-1)}{n+1}| \\\\  & =2|x-1|{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{n+1} \\\\  & =2|x-1|\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCondition of convergence $L<1$ is satisfied for all $x\\in I=(-\\infty ,\\infty )$, which is the interval of convergence in this case. The radius of convergence is $R=\\infty .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-10949/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfc0d9e1-bce1-5d62-b3c8-f7d7bb226497"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-10949"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-13912/selection/0a45858a305cf09d88b27c471e82d061648635fb6f2c04290610fda5f5a0ad2e" :answer/id #uuid "3cceb71f-d7c8-545e-aa1b-da9d0be4cc89" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R=1$ and  $I=(0,2]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13912/selection/e8e8c01b4c5259494051f2189be4b864c55e93e2b4aa9483952a548d0413e010" :answer/id #uuid "64cbf145-03f1-5fbd-ae61-a610ccd2e1bf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R=1$ and  $I=[0,2]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13912/selection/dff6684862eb71c7b1b3e3b98f09294701a43d9ad50fc4a2dcac9d83238357bd" :answer/id #uuid "a85a2725-9592-593f-a2f2-f265d597d1a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R=1$ and  $I=[0,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13912/selection/4cda7cd783e807714ba39243be65ad5faf7b14b0d6fc1549301bd76f413138ad" :answer/id #uuid "3386aa4f-1a8d-5a39-bf78-987f8bc4f2c1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R=\\infty $ and  $I=(-\\infty ,\\infty )$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13912/selection/ece93812d967d1ec58816d96e6d73871693d020c19dc84b6c8dd4b513b275ffc" :answer/id #uuid "53e34974-caa0-599e-8be0-4d193ed95a38" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R=1$ and  $I=(0,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-13912/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "91d818ba-bd42-5be3-b740-03c5c3181697" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-13912/selection/e8e8c01b4c5259494051f2189be4b864c55e93e2b4aa9483952a548d0413e010" :answer-field/choices ["q-13912/selection/0a45858a305cf09d88b27c471e82d061648635fb6f2c04290610fda5f5a0ad2e" "q-13912/selection/e8e8c01b4c5259494051f2189be4b864c55e93e2b4aa9483952a548d0413e010" "q-13912/selection/dff6684862eb71c7b1b3e3b98f09294701a43d9ad50fc4a2dcac9d83238357bd" "q-13912/selection/4cda7cd783e807714ba39243be65ad5faf7b14b0d6fc1549301bd76f413138ad" "q-13912/selection/ece93812d967d1ec58816d96e6d73871693d020c19dc84b6c8dd4b513b275ffc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-13912" :question/id #uuid "4c54e973-6e64-50b6-b096-4b16776e42ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-13912" :question/problem "Find the radius of convergence $R$ and interval of convergence $I$ for the series\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}}\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To apply the ratio test we define ${a}_{n}=\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}}.$ Then, we calculate the ratio of two successive terms and take the limit as $n\\to \\infty :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{(x-1)^{3(n+1)}}{(n+1)^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{{n}^{3}}{(x-1)^{3n}}| \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }|\\frac{{n}^{3}(x-1)^{3}}{(n+1)^{3}}| \\\\  & =|x-1{|}^{3}{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{n}{n+1})}^{3} \\\\  & =|x-1{|}^{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =|x-1{|}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe series converges if $L<1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x-1{|}^{3} & <1 \\\\ |x-1| & <1 \\\\ -1<x-1 & <1 \\\\ 0<x & <2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the radius of convergence is $R=1,$ and the series converges for any $x$ that lies in the open interval $(0,2).$\n\nThe ratio test gives no conclusion about the convergence of the series when $L=1.$ So, when $|x-1|=1,$ we do not know if the series converges. This means that the endpoints $x=0$ and $x=2$ need to be investigated separately using another test for convergence.\n\n- When $x=0$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & =-1+\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{4}^{3}}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis series is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\n- When $x=2$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(x-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(2-1)^{3n}}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{3}} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{4}^{3}}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis series is convergent by the $p$-series test.\n\nConsequently, the interval of convergence is $I=[0,2].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-13912/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bfc0d9e1-bce1-5d62-b3c8-f7d7bb226497"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-13912"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-50871/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "8f1d1bbd-5948-5b3f-bad9-c21f73b84442" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50871/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c22f9eb3-e464-5cb8-aacc-e302d005f5f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50871/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "9aeabdca-9c2d-5ebf-ad81-a61d33bf8eac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50871/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "4fa7366b-f3de-5758-830b-437ae25b3afc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50871/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "9c401994-b0bb-519d-9265-a62c93ede275" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50871/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "39c198d6-8d7c-57da-af05-12cae403c077" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-50871/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-50871/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-50871/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-50871/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-50871/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-50871/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-50871" :question/id #uuid "1407a663-14cb-5262-82d0-8dc686ad5604" :question/math-academy-id "q-50871" :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x-2)}^{n}$ converges at  $x=0.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n\n- The series converges at $x=1$\n- The series diverges at $x=4$\n- The series diverges at $x=-2$" :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=2,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=0,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $2,$ i.e., $R\\ge 2.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[0,4).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[0,4).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070319/assets/a56e24009403f0177f608ba932c03ab77e8db35e1db3e1221c4fb49efca7219f.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $1\\in [0,4),$ the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $4\\notin [0,4),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=4.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $-2\\notin [0,4),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=-2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-50871/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50871"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-50878"] :question/problem "The power series ${\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1.$ Which of the following **must** be true?\n\n- The series converges at $x=0$\n- The series converges at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$\n- The series diverges at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $\\frac{3}{2},$ i.e., $R\\ge \\frac{3}{2}.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[-1,2).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[-1,2).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070319/assets/03901ede0b4fadb59556c63aa4534b3a9e20c1e8188388e6256434ece03d9211.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $0\\in [-1,2),$ the series is convergent at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $-\\frac{3}{2}\\notin [-1,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-\\frac{3}{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $2\\notin [-1,2),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is divergent at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-103150/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "bbe935d6-4e1b-5f7e-8091-b06a6835a130" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103150/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "32282dea-b17d-5d30-8790-c81d3298c5fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103150/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "512ccae2-2ef3-5111-a276-1fc8cb7aef86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103150/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "703950ce-79f0-571a-a3ad-e8c92fc321e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103150/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9a0b5829-3986-50f2-a5ac-00aa4f84e6dd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103150/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "261de739-ef95-530e-af64-b6998f17f912" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103150/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-103150/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-103150/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-103150/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-103150/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-103150/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103150" :question/id #uuid "ec34b3f9-f746-52c7-8ca3-5de14cc8b3a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-103150" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+3)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-1,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n\n- The series converges at $x=-5$\n- The series converges at $x=-2$\n- The series converges at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-3,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-1,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $2,$ i.e., $R\\ge 2.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-5,-1].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-5,-1].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070319/assets/7d68a4bd81717c3ad663fc85c45dfce62217a046f683cc92a6869f87ff3b166a.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $-5\\notin (-5,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $-2\\in (-5,-1],$ the series is convergent at $x=-2.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $1\\notin (-5,-1],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-103150/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103150"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
